Scope: manifest (SP1.1.files) matches `git diff HEAD --stat` in the worktree exactly
(6 files: handlers_spending_optimizer.go, spending_optimizer_{test,render_test}.go,
models/spending_optimizer.go, models/whatif.go, spending_optimizer.html). Worked in
a `cp -a` copy at /tmp/claude-1000/sp1-checker-second; never touched the real tree
or :8080/:8091/:8098.

(a) Apply persists RAW form == saved SpendingSearch, unrelated settings unchanged:
  `go test ./internal/handlers/whatif -run TestSpendingApplySavesSearchPreferences -v -count=1`
  → 3/3 subtests PASS. This test explicitly poisons `p.request` with different
  values (99/5/6000/17000/100) than `p.form` (the case values) and asserts the
  SAVED SpendingSearch equals `p.form`'s values, not `p.request`'s — a strong
  mutation-kill against the split-classification-style bug of leaking the
  normalized request instead of the raw form. Confirmed live (see (e)).

(b) Defaults/strict-zero: `TestSpendingApplySavesSearchPreferences/defaults` →
  `&SpendingSearchPreferences{MaxShortfallPct:5}`; `/strict-zero` →
  `{MaxShortfallPct:0}`. Live-verified: POSTed max_shortfall_pct=0 through
  optimize→apply on a running scratch server (BUDGET_DATA_DIR=copied demo data,
  :8092); `whatif.json` after apply shows `"spending_search":{"max_shortfall_pct":0}`
  (advanced fields correctly omitted via omitempty; MaxShortfallPct has no
  omitempty so 0 is written). Reload showed `value="0"`, not blank or "5".

(c)/(d) Form-data keys and rendered values: `TestSpendingOptimizerFormRestoresSearchPreferences`
  (none/saved/strict-zero/fractional) and `TestSpendingOptimizerRenderSearchPreferences`
